  message: "emission-parity:F1 / G2 gate (PR #4202) adds the entrypoint_concept row: only the Python analyzer emits entrypoint concepts (Symbol.meta concepts list / usage_contexts); js/ts/go/java/rust/csharp/swift all emit zero — locked as strict-xfail (the js/ts fixtures carry a top-level entrypoint idiom so the cell is falsifiable, not construct-absent). This is the upstream cause of the dead-code-maybe Python monoculture. The Wave-3 per-language EP-concept emission fix will XPASS-trip these 7 cells. Stays todo_hard."  # 8db0
- op: discuss  # 9ef5
  at: '2026-06-24T09:24:33Z'  # 9ef5
  by: agent  # 9ef5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9ef5
  clock: 4  # 9ef5
  nonce: 9ef5  # 9ef5
  message: "Investigation (2026-06-24, lab notebook notebookjournal_06242026_0440.md) found the entrypoint_concept matrix-xfail framing was a MEASUREMENT ARTIFACT, not a real gap. The emission-parity matrix runs analyzers in isolation, but entrypoint detection is a PIPELINE concern: all 8 emission-parity fixtures already yield entrypoints in the full pipeline via four mechanisms (always-on main-functions.yaml -> main_function for go/java/rust/csharp/python; graph-structural script_module for js/ts; connectivity_based fallback for swift; python inline main_guard). Verified empirically via run_behavior_map on every fixture. Emitting entrypoint concepts inline per-analyzer would be redundant gate-gaming (duplicates the centralized convention layer; enrich_symbols would clobber it). Corrected the gate instead: restricted entrypoint_concept matrix applicability to python (its sole analyzer-level entrypoint concept), KNOWN_HOLES now empty (matrix at full parity), and added a pipeline-level gate test_entrypoint_parity.py locking the real cross-language invariant. Landing via branch jgstern-agent/refactor/entrypoint-parity-gate (merge pending Codeberg remote recovery; queued as vPR). WI-tosul STAYS OPEN, re-scoped to its actual substance: the dead-code-maybe Python monoculture is a COVERAGE problem (per-language framework/route detection breadth), distinct from entrypoint-existence."  # 9ef5
- op: discuss  # 2c8c
  at: '2026-07-02T04:20:02Z'  # 2c8c
  by: agent  # 2c8c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2c8c
  clock: 5  # 2c8c
  nonce: 2c8c  # 2c8c
  message: "RE-MEASURE GATE COMPLETE (2026-07-01/02) — user-approved 're-measure gate only' scope (not the XL sweep). Ran a bounded injected-fixture polyglot re-measure (top-5 langs, canonical web-route idioms, FULL pipeline via run_behavior_map — WI-rubip discipline, never self-substrate counts). Fixtures: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/fixtures/route-parity/.\n\nFINDING 1 — entrypoint-EXISTENCE is already gated (test_entrypoint_parity.py, all 8 langs; the emission-parity matrix entrypoint_concept column was reclassified python-only on 2026-06-24). So that half of the old premise is DONE, not pending.\n\nFINDING 2 — the REAL residual (per-language framework/route CONCEPT breadth = the dead-code 'Python monoculture' cause) is now MEASURED, and it is neither uniform nor simply-missing:\n- python Flask @app.route -> concept=route, but MANIFEST-DETECTION-GATED (fires only with flask declared in requirements.txt/pyproject; partly explains the monoculture since real py repos declare it).\n- rust actix #[get] -> concept=route, manifest-gated (Cargo.toml).\n- go net/http HandleFunc -> framework_role=route (analyzer-level; fires with NO manifest).\n- javascript Express app.get -> analyzer-level route_path/http_method meta (NOT a concept; no manifest).\n- java Spring @GetMapping -> NOTHING. Not a fixture artifact: spring-boot IS detected from the pom (verified live), spring-boot.yaml HAS the route pattern, and the analyzer extracts decorators=[{name:GetMapping,args:[/users]}] — yet enrich_symbols tags no route. Filed WI-tolap.\n\nCHARACTERIZATION — route detection is (a) 3-MECHANISM and inconsistently surfaced (concept vs framework_role vs analyzer route_path meta — an INV-numat-family axis question), (b) concept-level detection is MANIFEST-DETECTION-GATED (AUTO mode), and (c) at least java Spring is an outright BUG. So the WI-tosul sweep is NOT 'add per-language emitters'; it is: fix broken cases (WI-tolap), UNIFY the surfacing mechanism, and reconsider whether import-based detection (not just manifest) should trigger concept enrichment.\n\nGATE STOOD UP — test_route_concept_parity.py (dev 4c8339a079): per-language canonical route fixtures through the full pipeline; route detection (any of the 3 mechanisms) locked as hard asserts for py/js/go/rust; java strict-xfail -> WI-tolap. Gate-before-sweep ratchet: any breadth fix XPASSes and forces a flip to green.\n\nSTATUS — the wave3_remaining_plan §D 'GATED, do-NOT-implement-pending-re-measure' posture is now CLEARED: the residual is measured (not the frozen 99% premise), characterized, and gate-guarded. WI-tosul stays todo_hard for the actual sweep, now SCOPED by the above (natural first steps: WI-tolap java-Spring fix, then the surfacing-mechanism unification). Full re-measure writeup: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/wave3_tosul_remeasure_07022026.md."  # 2c8c
- op: discuss  # feb0
  at: '2026-07-05T03:29:50Z'  # feb0
  by: agent  # feb0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # feb0
  clock: 6  # feb0
  nonce: feb0  # feb0
  message: "Surfacing-consistency ADR DIRECTION resolved (human, adversarially stress-tested; the 'new typed endpoint sibling C' lean reversed). Target = D / CONSOLIDATE-ON-EXISTING: route-ness already has two canonical homes — EntrypointKind.HTTP_ROUTE (consumer-facing; entrypoints.py already ORs all three signals into one record) + the ADR-0027 route->function marker (producer-side: kind=function + meta.framework_role='route' + route_path/http_method). The ADR declares those canonical, promotes ONE accessor pair (is_route / route_of->{path,method,framework,protocol}|None) that ORs the three signals + NORMALIZES extraction, rewrites the ~5-7 duplicated OR-sites (cmd_routes/_route_json_record, _is_route_symbol, _extract_route_info, base.py widening, parity _route_detected) to call it, and documents meta.concepts[concept='route'] as the manifest-gated upstream projection. C rejected (route-ness boolean is edge-derivable per ADR-0027 Test 1 -> junid over-engineering; a new sibling = ADR-0044 redundancy leak). A rejected (concepts manifest-gated, darks go net/http + js Express). B rejected earlier (framework_role impure). PLUS (ii) additive payload normalization: additive registered meta keys route_framework (uniform across languages; today only on the concept dict) + route_protocol (split the WS sentinel out of http_method), normalized by route_of() — strictly additive, no new axis, no schema-structure break; producer emission work deferred (scope not build). SCOPE-OUT (non-blocking): the manifest-gating DETECTION dark (concept=route darks go/js) = WI-tosul coverage-breadth, which NO axis choice fixes; broader endpoint taxonomy (route_mount/controller/websocket_handler/grpc) = separate. STAYS todo_hard for the ADR-writing + accessor implementation (agent work; human direction extinguished). Provenance: decision_register_06102026.md UPDATE 2026-07-04."  # feb0
- op: discuss  # e2be
  at: '2026-07-07T09:29:26Z'  # e2be
  by: agent  # e2be
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e2be
  clock: 7  # e2be
  nonce: e2be  # e2be
  message: "STRATEGIC INVESTIGATION (4-angle parallel, pre-implementation) — WI-tosul is NOT an XL from-scratch per-language route sweep. It decomposes into 2 bounded chokepoints + a WI-tolap-shaped ratchet:\n\n1. route_of()/is_route() accessor (CHOKEPOINT, target-D, decided). ~15 read-sites in 4 files. NEW FINDING: a SECOND duplicate accessor pair exists in linkers/http.py (_has_route_concept:1531, _get_route_symbols:1564, _get_route_info_from_concept:1536) — a literal copy of cli.py's _is_route_symbol/_extract_route_info. Consolidation targets: cli.py routes family (_route_json_record:1934, cmd_routes:2004, dedup/sort/display extracts), cli.py slice/tier family (_is_route_symbol:8097, _extract_route_info:8128, tier promotion:8719), entrypoints.py (_detect_from_concepts:496, Pass-2 direct:1255), http.py duplicate pair, parity _route_detected. GOTCHAS: (a) EXCLUDE base.py _is_route_for_widening:1293 (identity/stable-id superset incl. route_mount + :route id-suffix + call_site exclusion — must NOT delegate); (b) KEEP marker-only predicates framework_role-ONLY (cli.py:8114 _is_route_marker, grpc.py:580, framework_patterns.py:1807/1829/1992 — ORing concept would break marker-vs-handler discrimination); (c) the two duplicate pairs have OPPOSITE precedence (cli prefers framework_role-first, http prefers concept-first) — pick framework_role-first canonical (ADR-0027 marker authoritative; concept = manifest-gated projection); (d) route_path/http_method are UNREGISTERED MetaKeySpecs — register them alongside the new route_framework/route_protocol.\n\n2. Monoculture root CORRECTED (Angle 2): dead-code-maybe ALREADY seeds routes language-agnostically (entrypoints Pass-1 concept + Pass-2 framework_role; go already anchors; route->handler dispatches_to already a reachability edge). So the accessor does NOT dissolve the monoculture. The monoculture is a DETECTION/GATING problem — non-Python route signals unevenly PRODUCED/GATED.\n\n3. Manifest-gating (Angle 3, CHOKEPOINT): the gate is ONE function refine_frameworks (profile.py:3143-3323), ONE condition (profile.py:3074, require_prefix_arm passed at 3271-3280). Making bare imports of route frameworks trigger concept enrichment = ~1-5 lines; the route-framework allowlist is DATA-DERIVABLE from the 71 concept=route YAMLs; PROMOTE already iterates frameworks generically (3253). Brute-force is confined to VALIDATION (35 frameworks, which bare tokens are FP-safe) — a bakeoff calibration, not per-language code.\n\n4. Per-language breadth (Angle 4, RATCHET not brute-force): WI-tolap is the archetype (detection+catalog+extraction all present; fix = broaden spring-boot import patterns, 0->35 routes). Tail languages share the shape — annotations/decorators already extracted, YAML present, generic engine matches — so each residual is a small per-framework matcher/gating fix, evidence-gated by the route-parity fixtures (which grow).\n\nPLAN: (1) build accessor [starting now], (2) manifest-gating relaxation + bakeoff calibration, (3) per-framework ratchet. Full 4-angle detail: workflow wf_d18de7d4-b4d."  # e2be
