  clock: 9  # 26f7
  nonce: 26f7  # 26f7
  message: "Phase-1b-β DONE + INV-tibap SATISFIED (merged dev 416f41fe6d). The transport-protocol FOLD (audit Pair-C) landed as one atomic ~15-site lockstep PR: WS/LIVE/RPC out of http_method into route_protocol; the entrypoints WS-dispatch (both concept + Pass-2 marker paths) now delegate to route_of + branch on protocol=='websocket' (the deferred Phase-1b-β), route_handler LiveView flag reads route_protocol=='liveview', 4 cmd_routes dict sites use protocol_method_token. Grounded on a 4-agent producer/consumer census + adversarial completeness check (protocol_origin reuse REJECTED — ADR-0031 Class-A/B biconditional; LIVE->liveview per human). So the ENTIRE surfacing-consistency arc (1a accessor + 1b-α framework-union/fold + INV-tibap/1b-β protocol-fold) is complete. REMAINING for WI-tosul: only the COVERAGE-BREADTH monoculture (Phase 2 manifest-gating relaxation in refine_frameworks, bakeoff-FP-calibrated; Phase 3 per-framework ratchet). WI-tosul stays todo_hard for Phase 2/3."  # 26f7
- op: discuss  # e5ca
  at: '2026-07-07T21:29:20Z'  # e5ca
  by: agent  # e5ca
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e5ca
  clock: 10  # e5ca
  nonce: e5ca  # e5ca
  message: "Phase 2 (manifest-gating relaxation) MERGED (dev 7efc74ec15). The dead-code route-monoculture ROOT is addressed: allowlisted route frameworks now promote on a bare EXACT import (from flask import Flask) even with NO manifest — previously refine_frameworks's bare-name arm required a compound-submodule import (WI-pusad), so a top-level import stayed dark. New _BARE_EXACT_PROMOTE_ROUTE_FRAMEWORKS allowlist (16: flask/fastapi/sanic/litestar/quart/starlette/bottle/tornado/pyramid/django/flask-appbuilder + express/koa/fastify + sinatra/padrino), one-line gate change (require_prefix_arm=(fw not in allowlist)); every FP-prone bare name stays gated (graphql/react/solid/plug/aiohttp/next). Grounded on the 3-agent Phase-2 scout + mini-trial (lab notebook phase2_manifest_gating_scout_07072026); the register's FP-prone hypothesis was corrected (grape/vapor/roda over-flagged; aiohttp/solid/nex were the real misses). Live-verified: Flask route no-manifest 0->1 marker+2 concepts. 7 existing tests updated for the new materialize-without-manifest behavior. 6804 tests pass, 100% cov.\n\nTAGGED awaits_bakeoff_validation: the quantitative claim (dead-code candidate Python-share drops from ~99% as manifest-silent / other-language route entrypoints start anchoring reachability) needs BROAD bakeoff before/after validation. Guard metrics: framework-FP count, WI-ronik http_route-on-frontend regression, route counts UP on manifest-silent web apps. Expand the allowlist (NEEDS-BAKEOFF middle set: aiohttp/falcon/grape/vapor/…) only in validated batches.\n\nWI-tosul REMAINING: Phase 3 (per-framework detection ratchet, WI-tolap-shaped, fixture-gated) + the allowlist expansion. Two independent latent blockers filed: INV-fosam (alias-mismatch, routes drop even WITH a manifest for next/adonis/aspnet/vertx/zio), WI-nizuv (coord-vs-namespace import patterns). WI-tosul stays todo_hard."  # e5ca
