  message: "Phase-2 BROAD before/after bakeoff DONE (pins 7b97443cf2 parent vs 7efc74ec15 Phase-2; profile.py is the ONLY runtime diff, so exact isolation; PYTHONPATH-pinned worktrees, per-run Phase-2-sentinel fingerprint guard; manifest-silent fixtures as positive control). VERDICT: mechanism VALIDATED (flask/fastapi/express/sinatra promote on bare-exact import, routes surface; ms_express JS dead 3->2 = non-Python route now anchors reachability, the WI-tosul thesis). FP guards VALIDATED — graphql/react/solid/aiohttp/next all stayed UNpromoted, frameworks_added=[]. NO collateral: 12 real repos / 7 langs / 1MB-141MB (flask-restful, gin, apollo-server, phoenix, spring-petclinic, vapor, fastapi, django, chatwoot, ...) ALL delta-zero (no wrong promotion, no dead-code regression, no reachability loss, no frontend-route FP). BUT corpus headline 'dead-code Python-share drops from ~99%' NOT demonstrated: Phase-2 fires only when a repo is manifest-silent AND imports the framework bare-ONLY (no submodule import — the pre-existing compound-submodule arm already handled those). Every real repo/subdir tested (incl. the manifest-silent backend/app subdir, which imports fastapi.routing/.security) is moot -> delta-zero. no_move at corpus scale, NOT a regression (change is correct+safe). Real corpus lever is INV-fosam (alias-mismatch drops route YAMLs EVEN WITH a manifest -> fires on the standard corpus, higher yield) + WI-nizuv + Phase-3; allowlist EXPANSION de-prioritized (same rare firing condition). Tag stripped. Full writeup: lab notebook wi_tosul_phase2_bakeoff_validation_07072026.md."  # 76d6
